        "id": 226184,
        "name": "payprplayn",
        "username": "payprplayn",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-30T13:52:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Argent adept, especially the Xtreme or Dark Conductor variants, are a natural for your theme, but might be just as op (though in an entirely different way).&nbsp; it might also be a non-problem. Remember the one-shots usually use a preset deck order.&nbsp; If you stack things right, I'm pretty sure you can give&nbsp;your original team a suitable challenge, though it may also subtract from the thematic time-manipulation feel you're drescibing.&nbsp; I think that may be your real issue here.&nbsp; In this game, any time you have a high degree of control, it usully means an easy victory.&nbsp; It seems like it would be difficult to acheive the experience you describe in a hard-fought game.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
